+pysemver sort
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+Sort versions, oldest first.
+
+.. code:: bash
+
+   pysemver sort [<VERSION>...]
+
+.. option:: <VERSION>
+
+    Versions to sort. If none are given, versions are read from
+    *standard in*, one per line; blank lines are ignored.
+
+The sorted versions are printed on *standard out* as plain text, one
+version per line, so the output can be read with a ``while read`` loop::
+
+    $ pysemver sort 1.10.0 1.2.0 1.2.0-rc.1
+    1.2.0-rc.1
+    1.2.0
+    1.10.0
+    $ printf '1.10.0\n1.2.0\n' | pysemver sort
+    1.2.0
+    1.10.0
+
+If any version is not a valid version, nothing is printed on standard
+out and the return code is 2.
+
+
+pysemver latest
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+Print the highest version that is not a prerelease.
+
+.. code:: bash
+
+   pysemver latest [<VERSION>...]
+
+.. option:: <VERSION>
+
+    Versions to check. If none are given, versions are read from
+    *standard in*, one per line; blank lines are ignored.
+
+The result is printed on *standard out* as JSON: a string, or ``null`` if
+there is no version, or only prereleases. Build metadata does not affect
+the comparison::
+
+    $ pysemver latest 1.2.0 1.10.0 1.11.0-rc.1
+    "1.10.0"
+    $ printf '1.0.0-rc.1\n' | pysemver latest
+    null
+
+If any version is not a valid version, nothing is printed on standard
+out and the return code is 2.
+
+
 Return Code
 -----------
 
